Job S03: premium_bands.sas. Parameters per run, in order: AsOfDate=2025-12-31.

Code:
 1 | /******************************************************************************
 2 |   Program  : premium_bands.sas
 3 |   Purpose  : Written and earned premium by line of business and premium band
 4 |              for the pricing committee. Each policy is banded once, on the
 5 |              premium of its first transaction as loaded, and all of its
 6 |              transactions are reported in that band.
 7 |   Inputs   : dw.fact_premium_earned
 8 |   Output   : rpt.premium_band_summary (rebuilt on every run)
 9 |   Params   : as_of - reporting date (SAS date), set by the scheduler
10 |   Author   : RN
11 | 
12 |   Change log
13 |     2016-02-22  RN    Initial version
14 |     2017-05-08  RN    Top band split: 1000 and over (CR-1077)
15 |     2019-10-14  CB    Transactions reported in their policy's band, not their
16 |                       own (CR-1520)
17 |     2022-03-07  CB    Policy count per band (CR-1951)
18 | ******************************************************************************/
19 | 
20 | /* premium bands used by pricing since 2017 */
21 | proc format;
22 |   value premband
23 |     low  -< 0    = 'NEGATIVE'
24 |     0    -< 250  = '0-249'
25 |     250  -< 500  = '250-499'
26 |     500  -< 1000 = '500-999'
27 |     1000 - high  = '1000+'
28 |     other        = 'UNKNOWN';
29 | run;
30 | 
31 | /* one row per policy: its opening transaction, as loaded */
32 | proc sort data=dw.fact_premium_earned(keep=policy_id lob_code written_eur)
33 |           out=work.opening nodupkey;
34 |   by policy_id;
35 | run;
36 | 
37 | data work.policy_band(keep=policy_id lob_code prem_band);
38 |   set work.opening;
39 |   length prem_band $8;
40 |   prem_band = put(written_eur, premband.);
41 | run;
42 | 
43 | /* every transaction, in its policy's band */
44 | proc sort data=dw.fact_premium_earned(keep=policy_id written_eur earned_eur)
45 |           out=work.txn;
46 |   by policy_id;
47 | run;
48 | 
49 | data work.txn_band;
50 |   merge work.txn(in=t) work.policy_band;
51 |   by policy_id;
52 |   if t;
53 | run;
54 | 
55 | proc means data=work.txn_band noprint nway;
56 |   class lob_code prem_band;
57 |   var written_eur earned_eur;
58 |   output out=work.premium_sums(drop=_type_ _freq_)
59 |          n(written_eur)=n_transactions sum(written_eur)=written_eur
60 |          sum(earned_eur)=earned_eur;
61 | run;
62 | 
63 | proc means data=work.policy_band noprint nway;
64 |   class lob_code prem_band;
65 |   var policy_id;
66 |   output out=work.policy_counts(drop=_type_ _freq_) n(policy_id)=n_policies;
67 | run;
68 | 
69 | data rpt.premium_band_summary(keep=lob_code prem_band n_policies n_transactions
70 |                                    written_eur earned_eur as_of_date);
71 |   merge work.policy_counts work.premium_sums;
72 |   by lob_code prem_band;
73 |   format as_of_date yymmdd10.;
74 |   as_of_date = &as_of;
75 | run;

Input tables:
- dw.fact_premium_earned: txn_id INT NOT NULL, policy_id INT NOT NULL, policy_sk INT NOT NULL, lob_code VARCHAR(5) NOT NULL, txn_type VARCHAR(4) NOT NULL, txn_date DATE NOT NULL, effective_from DATE NOT NULL, effective_to DATE NOT NULL, currency CHAR(3) NOT NULL, amount DECIMAL(12,2) NOT NULL, fx_rate DECIMAL(18,8) NOT NULL, written_eur DECIMAL(14,2) NOT NULL, term_days INT NOT NULL, earned_days INT NOT NULL, earned_pct DECIMAL(5,2) NOT NULL, earned_eur DECIMAL(14,2) NOT NULL, unearned_eur DECIMAL(14,2) NOT NULL, daily_rate_eur DECIMAL(12,4) NOT NULL, monthly_instalment_eur DECIMAL(14,2) NOT NULL, first_due_date DATE NOT NULL, as_of_date DATE NOT NULL

Semantic traps to test (one case per distinct trap id):
- SAS-12 (PROC FORMAT range boundaries) at lines 23-28: Each band includes its lower bound and excludes its upper one (-<), and '1000 - high' includes 1000. LOW does not match a missing numeric, so a missing written_eur falls to OTHER and gets 'UNKNOWN'. The CASE WHEN must spell out every boundary and send NULL to 'UNKNOWN'.
- SAS-09 (NODUPKEY keeps the first row in input order) at lines 32-34: NODUPKEY keeps each policy's first transaction in load order (the stable sort), and that row sets the band. Spark needs a window ordered by load order (_row_seq), not dropDuplicates.
- SAS-05 (MERGE BY with IN= flags) at lines 50-52: A one-to-many MERGE with an IN= subset is a left join from txn to policy_band. lob_code and prem_band come only from policy_band and stay missing for unmatched keys.
- SAS-05 (MERGE BY with IN= flags) at lines 71-72: A MERGE with no IN= keeps keys from both inputs, so it acts as a full outer join on lob_code and prem_band. Columns missing on one side stay missing, and the output is ordered by the BY keys.
- SAS-03 (Dates are numbers of days since 1 January 1960) at lines 73-74: &as_of is a SAS date number (days since 1960-01-01). In Spark it must be turned into a DATE, e.g. date_add('1960-01-01', as_of).
